          'Membership and payments: chosen plan, term, status and transaction reference. Card and bank details are handled by the payment providers; zuey.me does not store card numbers.',
          'Personal API keys: key name, scopes and usage details so you can manage and revoke keys.',
          'Zuey AI: the questions you send and the generated answers, stored per account so you can see your history.',
          'Consultation booking: name, email, the context you provide and the meeting time.',
          'Telegram community (Community plan): single-use invite links, your Telegram user ID once you join through such a link, and membership status so access follows your plan.',
          'Zuey AI on Telegram: your Telegram user ID is stored in the chat-account link table (channel_identities) when you link it on the /connect page, or carried over from joining the community group when that ID belongs to a single account. It is used only to check that you have an active plan before Zuey AI answers you on Telegram. Dewee (the platform running the bot) receives only an allow or deny decision and an anonymous reference, never your email or plan details.',
          'Weather (only if you turn it on): a city name or coordinates rounded to 1 decimal place (about 11 km). The choice is stored in your browser only; the server just forwards the query to Open-Meteo and does not link it to your account.',
          'Browser storage: a locale cookie (zuey_locale) and localStorage for the companion position and state, dismissed notices, recent commands, weather preference and the embed auto-load preference. You can clear these at any time in your browser settings.',
          'Usage analytics: page views and some interaction events (such as link clicks and language changes) via PostHog. Details and how to turn it off are in "Usage analytics" below.',
          'Technical logs: IP address, user agent and request details recorded by Cloudflare to operate the service and prevent abuse.',
        ],
      },
      {
        id: 'use',
        title: 'How data is used',
        items: [
          'To provide the account, paid content, Zuey AI, MCP/API, booking and community features you choose to use.',
          'To process payments, renewals and refunds and send transactional email (verification, receipts, reminders).',
          'For security, fraud and abuse prevention, and rate limiting.',
          'To understand aggregate usage and improve the product.',
          'To meet legal obligations.',
        ],
      },
      {
        id: 'isolation',
        title: 'Per-user isolation and administrator access',
        paras: [
          'Every API and MCP request is authorised against your own session or API key; one account’s data is not shown to another account.',
          'The administrator (Duy) has technical access to stored chats and account data. It is used only to provide support you ask for, to investigate security incidents or abuse, or when required by law. Administrator access to chats is recorded in an audit log.',
        ],
      },
      {
        id: 'ai',
        title: 'Zuey AI and model providers',
        paras: [
          'To generate answers, your question and relevant content excerpts are sent through the Dewee gateway to an AI model provider. Before that, TypeSafe AI may score which excerpts are most relevant to your question. These parties process the data to answer and may retain it under their own policies; zuey.me does not promise that providers never retain data.',
          'Do not enter passwords, secret keys or other sensitive information in the chat.',
        ],
      },
      {
        id: 'embeds',
        title: 'Content embedded from other platforms',
        paras: [
          'Knowledges articles and course lessons may embed posts or videos from X, Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, LinkedIn, YouTube, Vimeo, SoundCloud and Spotify. An embed loads automatically when you scroll to it. Your browser then sends a request directly to that platform, including your IP address, user agent and any cookies the platform has set, and the platform processes this data under its own policy. YouTube is embedded through youtube-nocookie.com and X in do-not-track (dnt) mode.',
          'You can turn automatic loading off on the device you are using with the “Không tự tải nội dung nhúng trên thiết bị này” (do not auto-load embeds on this device) button below any embed. Each embed then loads only when you click it. This choice is stored in your browser’s localStorage and is not linked to your account. A link to the original post is always shown.',
        ],
      },
    ],
    analytics: {
      title: 'Usage analytics',
      paras: [
        'zuey.me uses PostHog (a project dedicated to zuey.me, hosted in the US) to understand in aggregate which pages are viewed and which features are used. Each browser gets a random anonymous id stored in PostHog’s cookie/localStorage.',
        'When you sign in, that anonymous id is linked to your internal member id (a random string, never your email or name) so usage is not double-counted across pages. Signing out or deleting your account removes the link from the browser and starts a new anonymous id, so people sharing a device are never merged.',
        'Each event carries only properties declared in advance. Page addresses and referrers are stripped of sensitive parameters (such as token, code, email, key, secret, state, session) before sending; on account, payment and booking pages the whole query is dropped, order and booking codes in the path are replaced by a placeholder and the page title is not sent. Clicks inside survey, booking, checkout and chat forms are not recorded. Session replay is not recorded.',
        'Analytics does not run when your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, or when you turn it off here. The choice is stored in this browser; clearing browser data clears it. If your browser blocks local storage, analytics stays off too.',
      ],
      neverTitle: 'Never sent to analytics',
      never: [
        'Email address, name, avatar, phone number.',
        'Passwords, sign-in links, tokens, API keys, OAuth codes.',
        'Your Zuey AI chats, questions or prompts.',
        'Bank account numbers, card details, transfer memos.',
        'What you type into booking or survey forms.',
      ],
      controlTitle: 'Your choice',
      granted: 'Usage analytics is on in this browser.',
      optedOut: 'You turned usage analytics off in this browser.',
      dnt: 'Your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, so analytics is always off.',
      noScript: 'JavaScript is needed to change this choice.',
      optOut: 'Turn analytics off',
      optIn: 'Turn analytics back on',
      saved: 'Choice saved.',
      storageBlocked: 'Your browser blocks local storage, so the choice cannot be saved.',
    },
    processorsTitle: 'Processors',
    processorsIntro: 'zuey.me relies on the services below. Each receives only the data its function needs.',
    processorsHead: ['Processor', 'Purpose', 'Data involved'],
    processors: [
      { name: 'Cloudflare', purpose: 'Hosting, database (D1), CDN, security', data: 'All stored data, request logs' },
      { name: 'Resend', purpose: 'Transactional email', data: 'Email address, transactional email content' },
      { name: 'SePay', purpose: 'Vietnamese bank-transfer payments', data: 'Amount, transfer memo, transaction reference' },
      { name: 'Dodo Payments', purpose: 'Card payments (USD) for membership plans and courses', data: 'Email, name, zuey.me account ID and subscription status; card details collected by Dodo Payments' },
      { name: 'PayPal', purpose: 'Consultation payments (USD)', data: 'Booking reference, amount, payer name and email; payment details collected by PayPal' },
      { name: 'Dewee gateway and AI model provider', purpose: 'Generating Zuey AI answers', data: 'Questions, relevant content context' },
      { name: 'TypeSafe AI', purpose: 'Relevance ranking for search and Zuey AI', data: 'Search query or question, relevant content excerpts you can already read' },
      { name: 'Google', purpose: 'Sign-in; Google Calendar/Meet for consultations; Google Fonts', data: 'Basic sign-in profile; booker name and email; IP address when fonts load' },
      { name: 'GitHub', purpose: 'Sign-in; showing public activity of @mrgoonie', data: 'Basic sign-in profile. The activity section uses public events only, not your data' },
      { name: 'Telegram', purpose: 'Community plan groups; the Zuey AI Telegram bot; order alerts to the admin', data: 'Invite links, Telegram user ID, membership status, messages you send to the bot; order reference, amount, channel and transaction reference' },
      { name: 'Discord', purpose: 'Order alerts to the admin', data: 'Order reference, amount, channel and transaction reference' },
      { name: 'Dewee (Zuey AI Telegram bot)', purpose: 'Asks zuey.me whether a sender may chat with Zuey AI', data: 'Sender Telegram user ID and username; receives an allow/deny decision and an anonymous reference' },
      { name: 'Open-Meteo', purpose: 'Weather for background effects (optional)', data: 'City name or rounded coordinates' },
      { name: 'PostHog', purpose: 'Usage analytics', data: 'Page views, interaction events, the browser’s anonymous id, your internal member id once signed in (no email or name)' },
    ],
    processorsNote: 'If a new payment provider or processor is added, this list is updated before that service handles your data.',
    retentionTitle: 'Retention, backups and deletion',
    retention: [
      'Account, membership and chat history data are kept while your account is active or until you ask for deletion.',
      'Specific retention periods for each data type (chat history, technical logs, analytics) are to be finalised and will be published here.',
      'Infrastructure backups may still contain deleted data for a period before being overwritten; the exact period is to be finalised.',
      'Payment records may need to be kept longer to meet accounting and tax obligations.',
      'You can request deletion of your account and data by emailing hi@zuey.me. A self-service deletion flow is to be finalised.',
    ],
    rightsTitle: 'Your rights',
    rights: [
      'Ask to access, export or correct your personal data.',
      'Ask for deletion or withdraw consent (for example turn weather off or clear browser data).',
      'Revoke API keys and sign out sessions from your account page.',
      'Unlink Telegram from Zuey AI on your account page (Email & sign-in → Linked accounts), or email hi@zuey.me. Once unlinked, Zuey AI on Telegram stops answering that account; deleting your account removes every link.',
      'Complain to the competent data protection authority.',
    ],
    contactTitle: 'Contact and changes',
    contact: 'Send any privacy request to hi@zuey.me. When this policy changes materially, the effective date above is updated and the change is announced on the site.',
    back: '← zuey.me',
    pending: 'to be finalised',
  },
};

const c = content[lang];
const fallback = lang !== locale;
---

<Layout
  title={`${c.title} — zuey.me`}
  description={c.intro}
  url="https://zuey.me/privacy"
  lang={LOCALE_LABELS[lang].htmlLang}
>
  <main class="relative min-h-screen w-full flex flex-col items-center py-6 sm:py-12 px-2.5 sm:px-4 z-10">
    <article
      class="w-full max-w-[760px] bg-[#F5EFEB] rounded-[28px] border border-stone-200/90 shadow-floating-card px-4 py-7 sm:p-10 text-stone-900"
      aria-labelledby="privacy-title"
    >
      <a href="/" class="text-xs font-semibold text-stone-600 hover:text-stone-900 underline-offset-2 hover:underline">{c.back}</a>
      <h1 id="privacy-title" class="mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold font-serif tracking-tight">{c.title}</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-stone-600">
        {c.effective}: <time datetime={EFFECTIVE}>{EFFECTIVE}</time> · {c.authoritative}
        {fallback && <span> · {LOCALE_LABELS[locale].native}: English</span>}
        {lang === 'en' ? <span> · <a class="underline underline-offset-2" href="?lang=vi" hreflang="vi">Tiếng Việt</a></span> : <span> · <a class="underline underline-offset-2" href="?lang=en" hreflang="en">English</a></span>}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-800">{c.intro}</p>

      <nav class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/70 border border-stone-200 p-4" aria-label={c.title}>
        <ol class="grid gap-1 text-sm list-decimal pl-5">
          <li><a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-black" href="#pledges">{c.pledgeTitle}</a></li>
          {c.sections.map(sec => <li><a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-black" href={`#${sec.id}`}>{sec.title}</a></li>)}
          <li><a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-black" href="#analytics">{c.analytics.title}</a></li>
          <li><a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-black" href="#processors">{c.processorsTitle}</a></li>
          <li><a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-black" href="#retention">{c.retentionTitle}</a></li>
          <li><a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-black" href="#rights">{c.rightsTitle}</a></li>
          <li><a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-black" href="#contact">{c.contactTitle}</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <section id="pledges" class="mt-8 rounded-2xl bg-[#1c1917] text-[#f5efeb] p-5 sm:p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold font-serif">{c.pledgeTitle}</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
          {c.pledges.map(p => <li>{p}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>

      {c.sections.map(sec => (
        <section id={sec.id} class="mt-8">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold font-serif">{sec.title}</h2>
          {sec.paras?.map(p => <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-800">{p}</p>)}
          {sec.items && (
            <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-800 list-disc pl-5">
              {sec.items.map(i => <li>{i}</li>)}
            </ul>
          )}
        </section>
      ))}

      <section id="analytics" class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold font-serif">{c.analytics.title}</h2>
        {c.analytics.paras.map(p => <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-800">{p}</p>)}
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-bold">{c.analytics.neverTitle}</h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 grid gap-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-800 list-disc pl-5">
          {c.analytics.never.map(i => <li>{i}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <div
          id="analytics-consent"
          class="mt-4 rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white/80 p-4"
          data-granted={c.analytics.granted}
          data-opted-out={c.analytics.optedOut}
          data-dnt={c.analytics.dnt}
          data-opt-out={c.analytics.optOut}
          data-opt-in={c.analytics.optIn}
          data-saved={c.analytics.saved}
          data-storage-blocked={c.analytics.storageBlocked}
        >
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold">{c.analytics.controlTitle}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-700" data-consent-status role="status" aria-live="polite">{c.analytics.noScript}</p>
          <button
            type="button"
            hidden
            data-consent-toggle
            class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-stone-300 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold hover:bg-stone-50 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-amber-500"
          ></button>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="processors" class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold font-serif">{c.processorsTitle}</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-800">{c.processorsIntro}</p>
        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white/80">
          <table class="w-full min-w-[560px] text-left text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-stone-100 text-stone-700">
              <tr>{c.processorsHead.map(h => <th scope="col" class="px-3 py-2 font-semibold">{h}</th>)}</tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {c.processors.map(p => (
                <tr class="border-t border-stone-200 align-top">
                  <th scope="row" class="px-3 py-2 font-semibold">{p.name}</th>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">{p.purpose}</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 text-stone-700">{p.data}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-stone-600">{c.processorsNote}</p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention" class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold font-serif">{c.retentionTitle} <span class="ml-1 align-middle rounded-full bg-amber-100 border border-amber-300 px-2 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-bold text-amber-900">{c.pending}</span></h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-800 list-disc pl-5">
          {c.retention.map(i => <li>{i}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="rights" class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold font-serif">{c.rightsTitle}</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-800 list-disc pl-5">
          {c.rights.map(i => <li>{i}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold font-serif">{c.contactTitle}</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-stone-800">{c.contact}</p>
        <p class="mt-3"><a class="font-semibold underline underline-offset-2" href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a></p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  import { currentConsent, optIn, optOut } from '../lib/analytics/client';

  const root = document.getElementById('analytics-consent');
  const status = root?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-consent-status]');
  const toggle = root?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-consent-toggle]');
  if (root && status && toggle) {
    const label = (name: string): string => root.dataset[name] ?? '';
    const render = (note?: string): void => {
      const state = currentConsent();
      const text = state === 'do_not_track' ? label('dnt') : state === 'opted_out' ? label('optedOut') : label('granted');
      status.textContent = note ? `${text} ${note}` : text;
      toggle.hidden = state === 'do_not_track';
      toggle.textContent = state === 'opted_out' ? label('optIn') : label('optOut');
    };
    toggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const before = currentConsent();
      if (before === 'opted_out') optIn();
      else optOut();
      render(currentConsent() !== before ? label('saved') : label('storageBlocked'));
    });
    render();
  }
</script>
